<p>The United States issued a temporary, 30-day sanctions waiver that allows the delivery and sale of Russian oil and petroleum products already loaded onto vessels before March 12, a narrow easing that runs until April 11. US officials said the goal is to steady global energy markets after oil prices jumped following the Iran war. Several outlets said the waiver opens a short window for cargoes that were effectively stuck at sea to be sold and delivered.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/izsF3wSJoapmWxV4chisNo--lfLNW_wd6ZfQ_JueTtrdi_lS_NjLqGgQCM75-MfQCw-rW2EBD9q4T_9dD1NFwMuXVC1rAoTgEgxckNbnXiLWt3BFvruWitY2kLSkz3RsdbJoZLkMzSU4zEdszNncz4mGbuDlJgAsKUoT_wPBgBTRBzqzUYOJX4CqddPpgQEkHLfuQV2Deb5iykrQyZpkUC5ak_m5JLiM_5KS9iyLF0olPS8JC0MBtJkFzBNWhAnpqqii33YWA12FGA0YjQ' alt='A tourist watches the MT Desert Kite oil tanker carrying Russian oil at Narara Marine National Park in the Arabian Sea, Gujarat, India, March 11, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>India-like carve-out: Some reports described the move as expanding a carve-out previously linked to India to other buyers, as long as the Russian cargo was already at sea.</li><li>Economic backdrop: NDTV connected the waiver to broader financial strain, saying the Iran war has pushed up oil prices and rattled markets.</li><li>Cargo volume estimate: Around 19 million barrels of Russian crude and fuel on roughly 30 tankers in Asian waters were cited as potentially available for purchase.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent: Bessent said the waiver is meant to help stabilize energy markets unsettled by the Iran war. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/us-issues-30-day-sanctions-waiver-for-purchase-of-russian-oil-at-sea'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>US Treasury Department: The department issued a time-limited license that permits the delivery and sale of Russian oil already loaded onto vessels before March 12, effective for 30 days. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-temporarily-allows-sale-of-russian-oil-stranded-at-sea/a-76340827'>DW</a>)</li><li>The Hindu: The outlet said the license follows other steps aimed at easing energy pressure, including a Department of Energy announcement of a strategic petroleum reserve release. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-administration-takes-steps-to-ease-sanction-on-russian-oil/article70737840.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/us-issues-30-day-sanctions-waiver-for-purchase-of-russian-oil-at-sea'>US issues 30-day sanctions waiver for purchase of Russian oil at sea</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-temporarily-allows-sale-of-russian-oil-stranded-at-sea/a-76340827'>US temporarily allows sale of Russian oil stranded at sea</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-administration-takes-steps-to-ease-sanction-on-russian-oil/article70737840.ece'>U.S. grants India-like waiver to other countries to buy Russian oil</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/03/13/u.s.-temporarily-allows-sales-of-russian-oil-already-loaded-on-tankers-to-ease-energy-pressure'>U.S. temporarily allows sales of Russian oil already loaded on tankers to ease energy pressure</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-us-issues-30-day-sanctions-waiver-for-purchase-of-russian-oil-stranded/'>U.S. issues 30-day sanctions waiver for purchase of Russian oil stranded at sea</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/from-oil-price-rise-to-market-crash-iran-war-sparks-global-economic-jolt-11209723#publisher=newsstand'>From Oil Price Rise To Market Crash, Iran War Sparks Global Economic Jolt</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://globalnation.inquirer.net/313806/us-temporarily-allows-sale-of-some-russian-oil'>The United States treasury department issues a temporary license permitting the delivery and sale of Russian oil and petroleum products already loaded onto vessels before March 12, easing sanctions on such shipments until April 11 amid rising global energy prices.</a> - inquirer.net</li></ul>